---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Arrow from '../../../components/Arrow.astro';
import DisclosureIcon from '../../../components/DisclosureIcon.astro';
import MediaPlayer from '../../../components/MediaPlayer.astro';
import {nevermore, hasMedia, url, media} from '../../../lib/catalogue';
const moments=[
  {image:'host.webp', title:'Meet the Midnight Host.', text:'A figure emerges. A hand invites you closer. “Trick or Treat?” Your choice matters. What happens next is still a surprise.',alt:'The Skull Warden, Nevermore’s Midnight Host, extends an open hand.'},
  {image:'raven.webp', title:'Something heard you.', text:'Say “Raven” while armed and idle. A sweep, a watchful perch, perhaps something closer. The same word does not always bring the same encounter.',alt:'Azure Night raven in flight with detailed charcoal and cool-blue feathers.'},
  {image:'bride.webp', title:'Not everything is a scare.', text:'A spectral bride releases a butterfly. A chest offers a treat. Between the unsettling moments, there is room for something beautiful.',alt:'The Veiled Wraith Bride releases a butterfly from her open palm.'},
];
---
<Layout title="Nevermore — Halloween for AR Smart Glasses | GlassPlay" description="Arm a haunted Halloween mode. Meet the Midnight Host, choose Trick or Treat and summon the raven. Explore the Nevermore Windows and Raven Simulator preview." path="experiences/nevermore/" theme="nevermore" social={hasMedia ? 'media/nevermore/glassplay-social.webp' : 'brand/nevermore-social.png'}>
  <section class="nevermore-hero wrap" aria-labelledby="nevermore-title">
    <a class="back-link" href={url('#experiences')}><span class="back-arrow"><Arrow /></span>GlassPlay experiences</a>
    <div class="nevermore-title"><h1 id="nevermore-title">{nevermore.name}</h1><span>{nevermore.theme} · {nevermore.status} in preparation</span></div>
    <div class:list={['nevermore-hero-frame', {'title-art-frame':!hasMedia}]}>
      <img src={hasMedia ? media('cover.webp') : url('brand/nevermore-poster.webp')} srcset={hasMedia ? `${media('cover-small.webp')} 640w, ${media('cover.webp')} 1200w` : `${url('brand/nevermore-poster-small.webp')} 800w, ${url('brand/nevermore-poster.webp')} 1600w`} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 95vw, 90vw" alt={hasMedia ? 'Azure Night raven sweeps into the foreground, with the Midnight Host and Spectral Bride emerging behind it. A composition of approved production frames.' : 'Original 3D title artwork: a dark feather with restrained blue highlights.'} width={hasMedia ? '1200' : '1600'} height={hasMedia ? '630' : '1000'} fetchpriority="high" />
      <div class="hero-statement"><p>You armed something.<br /><em>Now it's here.</em></p><a class="button pale" href="#film">{hasMedia ? 'Watch the experience' : 'Explore the experience'}<Arrow /></a></div>
    </div>
    <p class="caption">{hasMedia ? 'Composition of approved production artwork. Physical Prism appearance has not been verified.' : 'Original title artwork. Gameplay preview is awaiting public release.'}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="story-intro wrap">
    <h2>Silence.<br />Presence.<br /><em>Then, an encounter.</em></h2>
    <div><p class="large-copy">Halloween isn't waiting on a screen.<br />It's waiting in your field of view.</p><p>Arm Nevermore and go on looking at your world. A pair of eyes. A shadow. A raven passing too close. Twenty authored encounters arrive with space between them, so anticipation has time to grow.</p><p>Some ask you to choose. Some simply arrive. You decide when it all ends.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="film-section wrap" id="film" aria-labelledby="film-heading">
    <div class="section-intro"><h2 id="film-heading">A glimpse<br /><em>after dark.</em></h2><p>{hasMedia ? 'Real production animation and a Windows capture in Raven Simulator Room. Play with sound for the full encounter.' : 'Discover the atmosphere and the encounters. The gameplay film will appear here once it is cleared for public release.'}</p></div>
    <MediaPlayer />
    {hasMedia && <details class="film-description"><summary>Read the film description<DisclosureIcon /></summary><p>The Azure Night raven flies close. The Midnight Host emerges from black, inviting a choice with “Trick or Treat?” A Mimic Chest opens, and the Spectral Bride releases a butterfly. Labelled Room sections show translucent encounters over a simulated kitchen. Cloth, wing sounds and the raven call accompany the action. This is an edited montage of encounters, not a continuous play session or footage from physical glasses.</p><a href={media('transcript.md')}>Read the complete transcript</a></details>}
  </section>

  <section class="moments wrap" aria-label="Nevermore encounters">
    {moments.map((moment,index)=><article class:list={['moment',{'reverse':index%2===1}]}>
      {hasMedia ? <img src={media(moment.image)} srcset={`${media(moment.image.replace('.webp','-small.webp'))} 480w, ${media(moment.image)} 960w`} sizes="(max-width:760px) 90vw, 50vw" alt={moment.alt} width="960" height="720" loading="lazy" /> : <div class:list={['moment-title-art',`moment-art-${index}`]} aria-hidden="true"><span>{index===0 ? 'Trick\nor Treat?' : index===1 ? '“Raven.”' : 'A strange\nkind of beautiful.'}</span></div>}
      <div><h2>{moment.title}</h2><p>{moment.text}</p>{index===1 && <p class="small-copy">Local voice recognition is available in the Windows preview. Physical Prism microphone behaviour is unverified.</p>}</div>
    </article>)}
  </section>

  <section class="ritual-section wrap" aria-labelledby="ritual-heading">
    <div class="section-intro"><h2 id="ritual-heading">An invitation.<br /><em>Never an obligation.</em></h2><p>No constant attention required. Nevermore leaves room for the real world, and always leaves you in control.</p></div>
    <ol class="ritual">
      <li><span class="ritual-number">1</span><h3>Arm the night.</h3><p>Choose ARM HALLOWEEN MODE. Nothing starts until you invite it in.</p></li>
      <li><span class="ritual-number">2</span><h3>Trick or Treat?</h3><p>Meet the Host. Choose, encounter, then return to silence.</p></li>
      <li><span class="ritual-number">3</span><h3>Call the raven.</h3><p>Say “Raven” while idle. Encounters respect pacing and cooldowns.</p></li>
      <li><span class="ritual-number">4</span><h3>Disarm. Instantly.</h3><p>Stop the video, audio and pending encounters. Your world is yours again.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="privacy-note"><h3>A haunting that stays with you.</h3><p>Encounters and voice recognition run locally. Listening is limited to the armed, idle experience. Normal operation does not retain microphone recordings. Discoveries are saved on your device.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="availability wrap" id="availability" aria-labelledby="availability-heading">
    <div><h2 id="availability-heading">Your first encounter<br /><em>is coming.</em></h2><p>Nevermore is in {nevermore.status.toLowerCase()}. The Windows / Simulator candidate has been tested; public downloads are not available yet.</p>{nevermore.install_url ? <a class="button" href={nevermore.install_url}>Get Nevermore<Arrow /></a> : <p class="availability-status">Download pending release approval</p>}<p class="small-copy">Version {nevermore.candidate!.version}. No sign-up or account required by the experience.</p><a class="text-link creator-link" href="https://github.com/RBraga01">Meet the creator <Arrow /></a></div>
    <div class="compatibility"><h3>Where it has been tested</h3><dl>{nevermore.targets.map(target=><div><dt>{target.name}</dt><dd>{target.label}</dd></div>)}</dl><p class="small-copy">Simulator footage shows a software preview. It does not establish the display, speaker, microphone, performance or thermals of physical glasses.</p></div>
    <div class="technical-details">
      <details><summary>Requirements & installation<DisclosureIcon /></summary><div><p>The preview is a Python application package, not a standalone executable. It requires Windows, Python 3.10 or later and a separately authorized Raven Framework 1.0.6 installation. A microphone is needed for the optional “Raven” interaction.</p><p>When released, the package will include runtime video, audio, the offline recognition model, checksums and installation instructions. Public downloads are not available yet.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Comfort & known limitations<DisclosureIcon /></summary><div><p>Nevermore contains sudden appearances, spiders and close creature encounters. Arm it intentionally, use a comfortable volume, and DISARM whenever you wish. Avoid use where distraction could be unsafe.</p><p>Prism uses an additive display: black contributes no light. Very bright real-world backgrounds can wash out dark detail. Room is the practical Simulator reference. Physical Prism testing is still pending.</p><p>Local keyword detection depends on the microphone and surroundings; a voice invocation may be ignored during playback or cooldown. Speech recognition on physical Prism has not been verified.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Credits & release status<DisclosureIcon /></summary><div><p>Nevermore brings together character artwork created with Meshy, animation authored for the experience, recorded Foley and generated character voices. Only finished rendered visuals are presented; original source models are not distributed.</p><p>The application is still being prepared for public release. The film shows the Windows / Simulator candidate.</p><a href={url('credits/#nevermore')}>Read credits and release information</a></div></details>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
